WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.933
First access should feel fast.

00:00:01.933 --> 00:00:04.252
Over-deliver in the first forty-eight hours.

00:00:04.252 --> 00:00:07.344
This lesson is about onboarding in 48 hours.

00:00:07.344 --> 00:00:08.504
Over-deliver first access.

00:00:08.504 --> 00:00:11.209
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.209 --> 00:00:15.075
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.075 --> 00:00:20.872
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.872 --> 00:00:25.124
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:29.376
Stay practical: write welcome message before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:34.409
Write a welcome message: what happens next, when, and how to reach you.

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:36.584
Remember the objective: write welcome message.

00:00:36.584 --> 00:00:40.572
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:40.572 --> 00:00:44.922
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:44.922 --> 00:00:48.910
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:53.260
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.798
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:55.798 --> 00:00:57.248
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:57.568 --> 00:00:58.733
Give access early.

00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:00.287
Delay creates buyer regret.

